  "description": "<p>Original report from Calvin:</p>\n\n<p>during our full 3million fedora3 object migration using the latest migration utility, at around 300,000 objects migrated got error message:ERROR 19:38:08.427 (Migrator) MIGRATION_FAILURE: UNREADABLE_OBJECT: message=\"java.io.FileNotFoundException: /fedora/data/objects/2013/0828/15/47/id-63560640R-pgimg-318 (Too many open files)\"java.lang.RuntimeException: java.io.FileNotFoundException: /fedora/data/objects/2013/0828/15/47/id-63560640R-pgimg-318 (Too many open files)       at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.next(FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.java:125) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.next(FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.java:38) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.Migrator.run(Migrator.java:148) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:265) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:58) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine.executeUserObject(CommandLine.java:1743) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine.access$900(CommandLine.java:145) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2101) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2068) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine$AbstractParseResultHandler.execute(CommandLine.java:1935) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at picocli.CommandLine.execute(CommandLine.java:1864) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.main(PicocliMigrator.java:145) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>Caused by: java.io.FileNotFoundException: /fedora/data/objects/2013/0828/15/47/id-63560640R-pgimg-318 (Too many open files)       at java.base/java.io.FileInputStream.open0(Native Method) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;na:na&#93;</span>       at java.base/java.io.FileInputStream.open(FileInputStream.java:219) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;na:na&#93;</span>       at java.base/java.io.FileInputStream.&lt;init&gt;(FileInputStream.java:157) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;na:na&#93;</span>       at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.next(FoxmlDirectoryDFSIterator.java:119) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span>       ... 11 common frames omittedFailed to list contents of /migration/coll/qafull0917/stagingjava.io.IOException: Failed to list contents of /migration/coll/qafull0917/staging       at org.apache.commons.io.FileUtils.cleanDirectory(FileUtils.java:1647)       at org.apache.commons.io.FileUtils.deleteDirectory(FileUtils.java:1535)       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:268)       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:58)       at picocli.CommandLine.executeUserObject(CommandLine.java:1743)       at picocli.CommandLine.access$900(CommandLine.java:145)       at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2101)       at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2068)       at picocli.CommandLine$AbstractParseResultHandler.execute(CommandLine.java:1935)       at picocli.CommandLine.execute(CommandLine.java:1864)       at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.main(PicocliMigrator.java:145)the command was /java-11-amazon-corretto/bin/java -jar /.stagedata/fedora6/migration-utils0917/target/migration-utils-4.4.1-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar --objects-dir=/fedora/data/objects --datastreams-dir=/fedora/data/datastreamstream --limit=60000000 --target-dir=/migration/coll/qafull0917/ --resume --source-type=legacy --debug -c</p>\n\n<p>I believe that the root cause is that FoxmlInputStreamFedoraObjectProcessor never closes its file input stream. It closes the xml read that operates on the input stream, but the reader DOES NOT close the underlying stream.</p>",
